I built the sprint board in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-contract-opus-3/app.contract` (two tab routes, three columns, a detail panel with its checklist, and an archive page). The data module is `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-contract-opus-3/app.ts`: its `overlay` shows each move, add, rename, archive, toggle and restore at once, and drops it by itself if the server declines. `./check` passes and all 26 visible tests pass with `./test`, using 2 of the 15 runs.

The part I was least sure of is error messages when several writes of the same kind are in flight. Contract's own failure slot would hide an earlier move's error once a later move succeeded, so `app.ts` keeps each kind's last refusal and the view reads it through an `errorsFor` resource; only the plain cases are tested, so this relies on how I read Exact's refresh rules. I also made two calls the brief doesn't settle: the rename field keeps its text after Rename, and after a successful write each affected column is fetched again from the server.